{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tc984yzonQQdiSQYjd1DZo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" reviewer scoring scale rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2021 - Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://2021.corl.org/reviewer-information/instructions-for-reviewers\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the official CoRL 2024 \"Instruction for Reviews\" page. Here's what I found regarding the reviewer scoring scale and rating criteria:\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Reviewer Expectations\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, as demonstrated by a record of previous publications in the area. Reviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period. Reviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results from the official CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page do not contain the specific numerical scoring scale (e.g., 1-10 ratings) or detailed rating criteria descriptions. The page content focuses more on the evaluation criteria and reviewer qualifications rather than the specific scoring system. You may need to access the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews directly to see if additional scoring details are provided there.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb8be02c-35b7-47dd-bfab-cb2c629ce5a2","uuid":"d14cda4f-5a26-4111-858c-b0b2b1401233","timestamp":"2026-05-13T03:13:00.317Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 \"instruction for reviews\" reviewer scoring scale rating criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BSnhMTPWh4ZNuJYSrURggv","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"Frequently Asked Questions","url":"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/"},{"title":"CORL 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2021 - Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://2021.corl.org/reviewer-information/instructions-for-reviewers"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the official CoRL 2024 \"Instruction for Reviews\" page. Here's what I found regarding the reviewer scoring scale and rating criteria:\n\n## Review Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Reviewer Expectations\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, as demonstrated by a record of previous publications in the area. Reviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals.\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period. Reviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results from the official CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page do not contain the specific numerical scoring scale (e.g., 1-10 ratings) or detailed rating criteria descriptions. The page content focuses more on the evaluation criteria and reviewer qualifications rather than the specific scoring system. You may need to access the full page at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews directly to see if additional scoring details are provided there."],"durationSeconds":5.906428687000004}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LGRgDzBvEpHCsPKWFP3Vtt","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL review form overall score rating scale 1-10 accept reject\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2021 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2021-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2022 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2022-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2021 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2021-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2024 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2024/ReviewerInstructions\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL reviewer guidelines, but the specific details about a 1-10 rating scale with accept/reject decisions were not fully detailed in the initial results. Let me search for more specific information about the CoRL review form scoring system.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/home\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://staging-dapeng.papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2024\"}]\n\nLet me try a more specific search to find the actual review form details with the rating scale.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2021 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2021%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2022 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2022%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Venues | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/venue?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL\"},{\"title\":\"Frequently Asked Questions\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/frequently-asked-questions/\"}]\n\nBased on my web search results, I was able to find some information about the CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning) review process, but the specific details about a 1-10 rating scale with accept/reject options were not fully documented in the publicly available search results.\n\nHere's what I found about the CoRL review process:\n\nThe main review part of the review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of this work. However, the exact numerical rating scale (1-10) and how it maps to accept/reject decisions was not detailed in the search results.\n\nThe search results indicate that CoRL uses OpenReview for its peer review system, but the detailed specifications of the overall score rating scale appear to be contained within the OpenReview forms themselves, which are not fully accessible through public web pages.\n\nTo get the specific information about the CoRL review form's 1-10 rating scale and how it translates to accept/reject decisions, you would likely need to:\n1. Visit the official CoRL conference website directly (such as corl2025.org or corl2024.org)\n2. Access the reviewer guidelines or review form documentation\n3. Check the OpenReview system if you have access as a reviewer\n\nIf you need this information for a specific year's CoRL conference, I'd recommend checking that year's conference website directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb8be02c-35b7-47dd-bfab-c