{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01TAe3b62W75CRAsMvmyVsEk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The specific CoRL scoring rubric isn't publicly available in detail. However, based on my knowledge of CoRL and robotics conferences, they typically use a 1-10 scale similar to other ML/robotics venues. Let me use what I know:\n\nCoRL typically uses a scale like:\n- 1: Trivial or wrong\n- 3: Clear reject\n- 5: Marginally below threshold\n- 6: Marginally above threshold\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n- 8: Strong accept\n- 10: Outstanding\n\nCoRL acceptance rate is typically around 30-35%.\n\n\nI'm identifying the key review dimensions—originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance, and limitations—and now I'm ready to dispatch the reviewers in parallel, with one focusing on methods and experiments while the other examines novelty and related work, then bringing them together through a structured roundtable process.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":66346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":702},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb8be02c-35b7-47dd-bfab-cb2c629ce5a2","uuid":"dec6054d-a2c0-4bf8-987a-417f72135f50"}
